{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm","id":893555,"title":"VTR fans, please explain how the Covenant from VTR are better than the Sects from VTM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-18T13:29:32-07:00","id":893555,"title":"VTR fans, please explain how the Covenant from VTR are better than the Sects from VTM","content":"OK, to tell everyone the truth I know very little of Requiem, I know that the Clans are a lot less important to the game and that Sects or Covenants play a more important role in a vampire existence. It's just the way I see it, everything you do in Requiem could be re-created in Masquerade. Although the Sabbat is there as a lurking enemy if playing a Camarilla game, in the end, well in most of the game I've played, you are mostly left to your own device as long as you don't interfere with the prince plans, don't break the masquerade and don't embrace without permission, you are free to do whatever you please. But it seem to me that, I just finish reading 1st edition part of the Covenant, and they come off to me as well, fanatic and I find them to very restricting and uninteresting.<br /> <br /> First you have;<br /> <br /> Carthian Movement: So basically is you hate status quo, and you want thing to change with a burning Ire you join this group.<br /> <br /> But what happens when you start getting power and feel that you might enjoy a bit of status quo in your life ? Your sect tell you, sorry man, but no status quo in this bitch, so you move on the Invictus... ?<br /> <br /> Then<br /> <br /> The Circle of Crone - bunch of Wackos venerating woman and deity who have been shun for their action and or belief and believe in creation so they are probably tending garden ( WTF !) or breeding animals or artist.<br /> <br /> Third<br /> <br /> Invictus - Seem to be written from without, with little to give, they pretty much tell you forward that your chance of increasing into the rank are slim to none, but you can try and until you do, you will be our pawn. - Some would say well camarilla isn't different, yeah, you don't need to be a prince to be powerful. In Masquerade, the Ventrue clan, protect their own, and don't have that stupid restrain oh, don't use technology like computer and cellphone and email, use messenger, its the tradition.<br /> <br /> Then<br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum - OK so we are fanatic catholic offshoot clan which reject humanity and assume the monster that we are, and human are cattle.<br /> <br /> They enforce/preach their faith, through violence if necessary, but oh wait what if our number are not great enough to convert the enemy, OK then will wait until we do. So if you want to be a religious fanatic with for a progenitor, the roman soldier that killed Christ, we got you covered.<br /> <br /> and Finally<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> Which attempt to transcend the vampiric state, and become something else superior.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and if you do not choose then you are unaligned and then everyone think of you like a bitch or less.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>So tell me Fan of VTR what exactly is it that makes VTR Covenant more interesting that VTM and its 2 Sect ? </b><br /> <br /> From where I am standing it seem a lot more limiting a setting than VTM was.. It was already hard sometime in my opinion to have all players find a reason for their character from different clan working together, now with so many different Sect/covenant, Not only are they probably from different clan but probably from different Sect which will probably not appreciate them aiding and or working with each other. All the while, I feel the clans have taken such a step back that I don't really see the point aside from each of them having a signature discipline and weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","user":"Arcaneumkiller","date":". 05-18-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:50:45-07:00","id":893573,"title":"","content":"I started Requiem with 2E, so I'm used to that take on Covenants and I don't know about 1E's presentation.<br /> <br /> I think the primary selling point of the Covenant structure is that they represent different ways Vampires make their night to night existence worthwhile beyond the mad scramble for blood.<br /> Some go for religion; some go for social activism or political power. A few try to try to see how far they can push themselves as Vampires.<br /> <br /> Each covenant gives context for your place in the world. The Lancea et Sanctum teaches that you're damned, but still have a place in God's plan. The Circle of the Crone tells you that the Beast is to be accepted as just another part of nature. The Carthians and the Invictus focus on what kind of society you're going to live in.<br /> <br /> One thing that I like about this is that every member of the coterie could be from a different Covenant. Another is that by specifying which groups are allied and in power, you can have more kinds of city structures beyond just Anarch/Cam/Sabbat cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:09:28-07:00","id":893587,"title":"","content":"For one? Diversity. Praxis under the Circle of the Crone is going to be a complete different animal than under the Invictus. The same is true with all the other covenants.<br /> <br /> Then you have the internal diversity. A Carthian domain could be an ode to fascism as much as it could be an experiment in the Mao brand of communism, or it it could be a democratic parliament.<br /> <br /> Secondly? There are more than 5 covenants. Seven? Belial's Brood? Tokyo's Zaibatsu? In Masquerade you have either the Anarchs, the Sabbath or the Ivory Tower. That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:09:38-07:00","id":893588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carthian Movement: So basically is you hate status quo, and you want thing to change with a burning Ire you join this group.<br /> <br /> But what happens when you start getting power and feel that you might enjoy a bit of status quo in your life ? Your sect tell you, sorry man, but no status quo in this bitch, so you move on the Invictus... ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Carthians are not about 'just' hating the status quo. It's about using the ideologies of the living to bring democracy to the All Night's Society. If you've managed that, and your domain now has a form of democracy, you're good. But democracy must be defended, as many of your buddies can subvert the will of others. If you know about the Anarchs, they might be considered a branch of the Anarchs in Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Circle of Crone - bunch of Wackos venerating woman and deity who have been shun for their action and or belief and believe in creation so they are probably tending garden ( WTF !) or breeding animals or artist. </div> </div> </div>I realize you say you don't know much about Requiem, and it's clearly true, but what you do seem to know is really limited and biased. The Circle of the Crone are about paganism, it's about embracing the fact that you are a vampire, a monster. Accepting that it's not a curse, it's a gift. After all, you were not cursed by god, either was the guy who turned you into a vampire. They can be seen as scary because most of the other covenants work on limiting or resisting their vampire nature, while the Circle embraces it.<br /> <br /> You can tend gardens or breed animals or be an artist in any covenant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invictus - Seem to be written from without, with little to give, they pretty much tell you forward that your chance of increasing into the rank are slim to none, but you can try and until you do, you will be our pawn. - Some would say well camarilla isn't different, yeah, you don't need to be a prince to be powerful. In Masquerade, the Ventrue clan, protect their own, and don't have that stupid restrain oh, don't use technology like computer and cellphone and email, use messenger, its the tradition. </div> </div> </div>The Invictus is most like the Camarilla. They have their hierarchy and tradition, and it's entirely possible to climb your way up to Prince or head of the Invictus in your city. There's no restraint not to use technology, but the Invictus also enforces the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lancea Sanctum - OK so we are fanatic catholic offshoot clan which reject humanity and assume the monster that we are, and human are cattle.<br /> <br /> They enforce/preach their faith, through violence if necessary, but oh wait what if our number are not great enough to convert the enemy, OK then will wait until we do. So if you want to be a religious fanatic with for a progenitor, the roman soldier that killed Christ, we got you covered. </div> </div> </div>They believe they're a very specific kind of monster. They're demons, cursed people put there to test and torment humanity so the kine can appreciate Virtue or Faith in God. As nice as they think it would be if they were in power, all they need is to be able to talk, and even if their covenant doesn't have the Prince or even a lot of power, they can preach and spread the word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> Which attempt to transcend the vampiric state, and become something else superior. </div> </div> </div>Overcoming the weaknesses and drawbacks, as well as taking advantage of the powers they grant, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh and if you do not choose then you are unaligned and then everyone think of you like a bitch or less. </div> </div> </div>Not really. You can be unaligned and an ally of other covenants. If 'everyone' treats you poorly you can just show them differently in time.<br /> <br /> You seem to be trying to start an argument but in case you're actually just interested in finding out about the covenants and what they offer that's different, here you go. Above you said that while the Sabbat are supposed to be at war with you, you can generally just do your own thing. In Requiem there is no Sabbat, and you are free to do your own thing, and ideally your philosophy as a vampire will fit into one of the covenants. Do you want power within a hierarchy, to be part of the established and dominant? Then the Invictus is on your side. Do you think being a vampire is not that bad, that you want to have fun with your immortality? Then join the Circle of the Crone. Did turning into a vampire open your eyes to limitless potential, do you think you could overcome the weaknesses of it and become something incredibly powerful? Then the Ordo Dracul is good for you.<br /> <br /> But beyond your covenant, you do what you want. It's your Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:17:48-07:00","id":893591,"title":"","content":"The Sects in Masquerade were all about choosing sides in an ancient war between, and about whether or not you wanted to cling to your Humanity. Requiem has moved away from the former and emphasized the latter, with the Covenants existing primarily as support structures for campires to hold onto through the long eternity of unlife. Covenants shape the beliefs that help keep someone relatively sane as they spend an immortal lifespan as a cruel predator, without which they would quickly fall to the Beast and become a ravening monster. Thr Covenants are there to answer the question of &quot;what do I do now?&quot;<br /> <br /> For the Invictus and Carthians, the answer they provide is political. The Invictus sees opportunity in their unnaturally long lives, pursuing worldly influence and wealth through the long night of the Kindred experience; they also focus on maintaining their Humanity with oaths of obligation and with petty politics, zooming in on ultimately meaningless titles as a distraction from being a mindless hungry beast. The Carthians hone in on mortal feelings of oppression and injustice, allowing passionate and politically active Kindred an outlet for their fury and frustration that isn't just murder and anarchy in the streets; it gives them hope for a better future with less social heirarchy and perhaps even a chance to do away with the Masquerade and return to something resembling normalcy. <br /> <br /> For the Lancea Sanctum and Circle of the Crone, the answer they provide is spiritual. The Embrace is a jarring, horrifying experience, and many feel lost as they must now turn to actions they would've found morally reprehensible in life in order to survive. Both of these Sects explain that it's okay go be a monster, assuaging feelings of guilt with either a divine purpose from the God Himself or a more general pagan belief structure that varies wildly. It's about acceptance and religious succor, distracting the hungry Beast with a new goal in (un)life and a new dogma to base one's identity and actions around.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul are the odd ones out in this equation, and are the smallest Covenant because of this. Rather than pretend at being human like the political factions or embrace the Kindred faiths, they instead fixate on the transformative act of the Embrace and seek to change themselves even further, but this time under their own direct guidance. The Ordo offers control, freeing a vampire to try and shape their own existence with hard work and giving them a goal to strive towards.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a more VtM-centric answer, I'd have to say that it had one interesting Sect - the Sabbat - while the Camarilla and Anarchs were played as both the boring default option (compare the number of clans and bloodlines in the Sabbat to those of the Cammies) and as the idiotic dupes of the setting (who bury their heads in the sand and pretend Gehenna isn't real) - while VtR presents all five Covenants as being equally compelling, diverse, and storied. Another major benefit is that you can bring together a coterie across Covenant lines, because they're all competing belief systems rather than outright warring factions; that tension offers far more story potential than &quot;if you see the other team, you kill them on sight.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:30:28-07:00","id":893605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893587#post893587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one? Diversity. Praxis under the Circle of the Crone is going to be a complete different animal than under the Invictus. The same is true with all the other covenants.<br /> <br /> Then you have the internal diversity. A Carthian domain could be an ode to fascism as much as it could be an experiment in the Mao brand of communism, or it it could be a democratic parliament.<br /> <br /> Secondly? There are more than 5 covenants. Seven? Belial's Brood? Tokyo's Zaibatsu? In Masquerade you have either the Anarchs, the Sabbath or the Ivory Tower. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are concise arguments presenting the best points to answer the Original Post's question. +1 Internet to you.<br /> <br /> I would add that the new Covenant system much better represent the use of organizations as coping mechanisms to a traumatic transformation to something alien from previous life experience, and trying to deal with how that separates them from known social coping mechanisms for stress and loneliness. Two Covenants busy themselves with distracting politics, one seeks solace in fulfilling their divine role via the Judo-Christian paradigm of God's sovereignty, another seeks meaning in a unified collection of alternative spiritual practices, and one Covenant driven by a self-improvement paradigm (Very similarly to many Path found in the Sabbat).<br /> <br /> You'll see echoes of the coping mechanisms used in the three Sects of VtM in the Covenants of VtR, but because there are more Covenants than Sects, you don't have weird pairing of groups that don't share the same motivation and the schisms which would occur if it wasn't artificially held together via the flimsy baling-wire of the pen-strokes of white wolf writers.<br /> The welding of spirituality and political war verses pragmatic materialism is a very valid storytelling metaphor (and is currently relevant for social commentary due to the Violent Islamic Extremist struggling against the passive-aggressive onslaught of Corporate Westernized marketing) and is the heart of the two primary Sects conflict of VtM.<br /> VtR, on the other hand, doesn't galvanize the conflict between materialism verses spirituality by reducing every significant dispute as a loose dichotomy in nature and instead makes a much more nuanced interplay between several interests, reflecting greater complexity than an mere &quot;our side or your side&quot; conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 05-18-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:35:35-07:00","id":893611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, to tell everyone the truth I know very little of Requiem, I know that the Clans are a lot less important to the game and that Sects or Covenants play a more important role in a vampire existence. It's just the way I see it, everything you do in Requiem could be re-created in Masquerade. Although the Sabbat is there as a lurking enemy if playing a Camarilla game, in the end, well in most of the game I've played, you are mostly left to your own device as long as you don't interfere with the prince plans, don't break the masquerade and don't embrace without permission, you are free to do whatever you please. But it seem to me that, I just finish reading 1st edition part of the Covenant, and they come off to me as well, fanatic and I find them to very restricting and uninteresting.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Covenants are more important then Clans 'as political structures' becuase in Requiem the Clans aren't political structures. In fact, in a lot of ways for this topic you shouldn't be comparing the Covenants to the Camarilla, but to the Clans. Their Masquerade political structure is closer to the Covenants. You should think of it this way, the Camiralla doesn't exist, Covenants replace the political aspects of Clans, and Clan just defines what kind of Vampire you are.<br /> <br /> They are only as fanatic as you portray them. As you said with the Cam vs Sabbat (or Clan), in most games they are just a Backdrop of groups that the characters likely belong to and have some association with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First you have;<br /> <br /> Carthian Movement: So basically is you hate status quo, and you want thing to change with a burning Ire you join this group.<br /> <br /> But what happens when you start getting power and feel that you might enjoy a bit of status quo in your life ? Your sect tell you, sorry man, but no status quo in this bitch, so you move on the Invictus... ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The don't dislike the concept of status quo, just the current status quo (IE The Invictus are in charge and use a rigid structure to control everyone).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then<br /> <br /> The Circle of Crone - bunch of Wackos venerating woman and deity who have been shun for their action and or belief and believe in creation so they are probably tending garden ( WTF !) or breeding animals or artist.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Religous =\\= fanatic, especially in a world where you know there is supernatural things (like being a vampire yourself). As Octavo said, its about context, for some people the idea of vampires as part of the natural cycle is how they would cope. (and others join the Circle for the benifits of their magic while just paying lip service to the religious aspects).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Third<br /> <br /> Invictus - Seem to be written from without, with little to give, they pretty much tell you forward that your chance of increasing into the rank are slim to none, but you can try and until you do, you will be our pawn. - Some would say well camarilla isn't different, yeah, you don't need to be a prince to be powerful. In Masquerade, the Ventrue clan, protect their own, and don't have that stupid restrain oh, don't use technology like computer and cellphone and email, use messenger, its the tradition.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Invictus are in some ways more like the Ventrue (Masquerade-style) in that regard more than the Camiralla.<br /> <br /> Also, I suggest switching to the second edition book. There has been a decade of development on these things that you are missing out on. The no tech thing was dropped becuase yeah its not really the best way to represent the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then<br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum - OK so we are fanatic catholic offshoot clan which reject humanity and assume the monster that we are, and human are cattle.<br /> <br /> They enforce/preach their faith, through violence if necessary, but oh wait what if our number are not great enough to convert the enemy, OK then will wait until we do. So if you want to be a religious fanatic with for a progenitor, the roman soldier that killed Christ, we got you covered.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of a reductive way to put it but yeah... They are vampires that believe (or pretend to for other reasons) in a semi-christian based doctrine and use some catholic trappings for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> and Finally<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> Which attempt to transcend the vampiric state, and become something else superior.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, reductive but essentially accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh and if you do not choose then you are unaligned and then everyone think of you like a bitch or less.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say what they thing, is that they can't trust you, they don't know where you allegiances are or what your motives might be (even more than normal).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>So tell me Fan of VTR what exactly is it that makes VTR Covenant more interesting that VTM and its 2 Sect ? </b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, I think this is really the wrong way to look at it. The covenets represent different groups of vampires with like minded thinking that more or less get along. They are definetly not at war with each other. Even the Invictus and Carthians are often (cause it varies from place to place) closer to the Anarchs and Camirilla than the Sabbat and either of those two. I'm not sure if it was introduced before somewhere in the line, but in 2nd Edition core at least, you can have status with more than one Covenent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From where I am standing it seem a lot more limiting a setting than VTM was.. It was already hard sometime in my opinion to have all players find a reason for their character from different clan working together, now with so many different Sect/covenant, Not only are they probably from different clan but probably from different Sect which will probably not appreciate them aiding and or working with each other. All the while, I feel the clans have taken such a step back that I don't really see the point aside from each of them having a signature discipline and weakness.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Your clan point is kinda the thing here. In Requiem, if you want to play a Gangrel that uses Blood magick, you can; by being a Circle of the crone or Lance, or you can be a Nosferatu that rules from the top of the Invictus through fear rather than hiding in the shadows. And as before, the covenets can work together fine, and the clans are literally, absolutley not a barrier to two vamps being around each other becasue there isnt ANY political attachment to them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Took too long to reply and a couple others did, but, what they said too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 05-18-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:42:57-07:00","id":893620,"title":"","content":"I look at the structure of Vampiric society in Requiem in general as a de facto Camarilla when the covenants are at least agreeing to disagree with a minimum of violence. I like the fact that your clan, the part of your character's origin they don't get a say in, does not wholly dictate the course of their life and philosophy as it does in Masquerade. The covenants, which are entirely optional, provide an extra dimension to the character to explore and 4+ different approaches to being undead and meeting night to night survival needs. If you want to play a Lasombra in Masquerade who despises the Sabbat and the theology of Caine, then your character automatically has to play through at least some degree of suspicion and intolerance from Anarchs or Camarilla. When 99% of your clan, which you had no choice in joining, is antagonistic towards the rest of Vampire civilization, its highly restrictive of your choices of character arcs as a player. Play the struggle of being branded a traitor and likely spy or choose a different concept because a setting in which a Lasombra can be Cam or Anarch without a lot of fear and suspicion that may be undesirable for the player is very, very niche and very difficult for the ST to contrive.<br /> <br /> In this way Requiem is more flexible game in terms of what characters you can play and how you choose to play them. However the clan archetypes in Masquerade and their rich, detailed histories work for Masquerade so that's a plus if you want a very good idea of what you're dealing with just by knowing what someone's clan is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:44:49-07:00","id":893624,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for replying<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893588#post893588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You seem to be trying to start an argument but in case you're actually just interested in finding out about the covenants and what they offer that's different, here you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I don't/didn't mean to come off in a rude matter or offensive although I was of sort going for a debate of sort, I was interested in people telling me their opinion, from their own experience they think, these covenant are so great. Trying to convince myself that the Covenants are OK, because just reading them, I thought they were awful, but I thought well maybe if I read some opinion and experience I might be able to see it differently by reading others post, and then debate the pro and cons of it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893588#post893588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But beyond your covenant, you do what you want. It's your Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they wanted us to see it more like a full time job, like you are a Lancea Sanctum, so don't let us catch you not advancing furthering the cause of the Sect, or not preaching or you are in big trouble.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893588#post893588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Invictus is most like the Camarilla. They have their hierarchy and tradition, and it's entirely possible to climb your way up to Prince or head of the Invictus in your city. There's no restraint not to use technology, but the Invictus also enforces the Masquerade.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>OK, well maybe this was retcon in 2nd Edition but the following is taken directly from the source material VTM 1st Edition Page 56;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Old-Fashioned Communication<br /> As an offshoot of the formality issue, many elder Invictus insist that most of their correspondence be conducted through the use of messengers or written letters. Telephones and email are considered gauche, the tools of an unlettered and ill -mannered youth. (Additionally, many elders are rightfully concerned that they don\u2019t know enough to protect themselves from outside eavesdropping.) Most elders aren\u2019t foolish about this protocol. When it comes to vital news or emergencies, they don\u2019t object to receiving a call or an email (though even then, Princes often prefer their Seneschals or other servants to receive the information and then deliver it in person). Using these techniques for any other purpose, however, is grounds for a social snubbing at the very least. (Some young Kindred claim that this \u201ctradition\u201d actually exists only so that elders aren\u2019t forced to reveal how uncomfortable and incompetent they are with modern appliances. They rarely make this claim in front of their elders, though.) </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893588#post893588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I realize you say you don't know much about Requiem, and it's clearly true, but what you do seem to know is really limited and biased. The Circle of the Crone are about paganism, it's about embracing the fact that you are a vampire, a monster. Accepting that it's not a curse, it's a gift. After all, you were not cursed by god, either was the guy who turned you into a vampire. They can be seen as scary because most of the other covenants work on limiting or resisting their vampire nature, while the Circle embraces it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yeah, all these years I have already remained with VTM, but every once in a while I try to learn again from Requiem but so many things are just... About the paganism I got that and when I was reading the crone description section, they where emphasizing on them being scary and embracing their vampire nature, but then you get the Lancea Sanctum, which are just equally inhuman in which they seem themselves complete predator over the kine and then you have Ordo Dracul which seem to want to transcend vampirism. and become something greater. From my point of view all three covenant are equally terrifying.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893588#post893588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can tend gardens or breed animals or be an artist in any covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is taken directly from the book 1st Edition page p.50-51<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Acolytes practice this ideology in small ways, tending gardens or breeding animals... </div> </div> </div>I understand that an Invictus could also be tending to a garden or any vampire, it's just...I was like really...Vampire obsess with creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893588#post893588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In Requiem there is no Sabbat, and you are free to do your own thing, and ideally your philosophy as a vampire will fit into one of the covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't VII, requiem version of the Sabbat? from what I understand, they seem to be somewhat similar. I haven't read the VII section yet in the book thought so I am really asking ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","user":"Arcaneumkiller","date":". 05-18-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:48:59-07:00","id":893633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cowardly Scion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893620#post893620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you want to play a Lasombra in Masquerade who despises the Sabbat and the theology of Caine, then your character automatically has to play through at least some degree of suspicion and intolerance from Anarchs or Camarilla. When 99% of your clan, which you had no choice in joining, is antagonistic towards the rest of Vampire civilization, its highly restrictive of your choices of character arcs as a player. Play the struggle of being branded a traitor and likely spy or choose a different concept because a setting in which a Lasombra can be Cam or Anarch without a lot of fear and suspicion that may be undesirable for the player is very, very niche and very difficult for the ST to contrive.</div> </div> </div> </div>So very true, I hadn't thought about it that way...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:56:00-07:00","id":893636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893624#post893624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought they wanted us to see it more like a full time job, like you are a Lancea Sanctum, so don't let us catch you not advancing furthering the cause of the Sect, or not preaching or you are in big trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how big a change it is from Masquerade but you can decide how devoted you want to be to your covenant. You're likely to get more status in the Lancea et Sanctum if you are full-fledged hellfire and brimstone preacher, but you can just go to services and offer lip service and have a place to belong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Old-Fashioned Communication </div> </div> </div>Yes that's something that was more prevalent in the beginnings of first edition but isn't really in second.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yeah, all these years I have already remained with VTM, but every once in a while I try to learn again from Requiem but so many things are just... About the paganism I got that and when I was reading the crone description section, they where emphasizing on them being scary and embracing their vampire nature, but then you get the Lancea Sanctum, which are just equally inhuman in which they seem themselves complete predator over the kine and then you have Ordo Dracul which seem to want to transcend vampirism. and become something greater. From my point of view all three covenant are equally terrifying. </div> </div> </div>It's terrifying being a vampire, but they have very different motivations between them. A member of the Lancea is doing the work of God, while an acolyte of the Crone is doing what comes natural, and a member of the Ordo Dracul is trying to find a way to better things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is taken directly from the book 1st Edition page p.50-51<br /> <br /> Some Acolytes practice this ideology in small ways, tending gardens or breeding animals...<br /> <br /> I understand that an Invictus could also be tending to a garden or any vampire, it's just...I was like really...Vampire obsess with creation. </div> </div> </div>The idea is that they are a natural part of the world. This doesn't mean they're all hippies or druids, but that they can still create things. They're not corpse machines fueled by blood, they're part of the world as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isn't VII, requiem version of the Sabbat? from what I understand to seem to be somewhat similar. I haven't read the VII section yet in the book thought so I am really asking ? </div> </div> </div>Not really. There was three different versions of them in first edition but none of them were really comparable to the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:22:55-07:00","id":893658,"title":"","content":"I guess a big part of my misconception was that once you join a covenant, you are kinda expected to do so many ritual for your covenant and are expected to be involve with your covenant, and I was like what if I don't give a **** about the vampire communities. What if I am just a vampire, a Ventrue, who expect to open multiple franchise and become rich, I care for a few of my clan brethren, my sire, and maybe a few of my ally and contact without which this might not be possible. I thought OK guess I would find myself being an Invictus, but then I read about the impossibility of gaining rank in the covenant, and then about the technology although you guys have confirm to me that this was retcon in 2nd edition which is a good thing.<br /> <br /> OK so now the clan are not so much a group anymore so I might not really increase within my clan, the Camarilla doesn't exist , and the only thing to gain rank into is bloated with Elders which are not ready to share power. I never care for anarchist movement and everyone is equal, not really my thing, so Carthian was not really likely. Believing pagan myth, being one with nature was really never happening, the Lancea Sanctum are equally way too fanatic for my taste, then there was the Ordo Dracul. But then again, I thought, if you had to be like a Tzimisce obsess with transformation and shit, transcending and metamorphosis hell no. I thought, while my vampire could be interested in controlling the best and not being control by it, I can't imagine he would spend any significant amount of time joining an association bent on transcending.<br /> <br /> So maybe my character would be unaligned, but I was like, is unaligned not the new - Caitiff of Requiem, where everyone is suspicious and would prefer you dead than walking. (Pun intended)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:38:40-07:00","id":893675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893658#post893658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess a big part of my misconception was that once you join a covenant, you are kinda expected to do so many ritual for your covenant and are expected to be involve with your covenant, and I was like what if I don't give a **** about the vampire communities. What if I am just a vampire, a Ventrue, who expect to open multiple franchise and become rich, I care for a few of my clan brethren, my sire, and maybe a few of my ally and contact without which this might not be possible. I thought OK guess I would find myself being an Invictus, but then I read about the impossibility of gaining rank in the covenant, and then about the technology although you guys have confirm to me that this was retcon in 2nd edition which is a good thing.<br /> <br /> OK so now the clan are not so much a group anymore so I might not really increase within my clan, the Camarilla doesn't exist , and the only thing to gain rank into is bloated with Elders which are not ready to share power. I never care for anarchist movement and everyone is equal, not really my thing, so Carthian was not really likely. Believing pagan myth, being one with nature was really never happening, the Lancea Sanctum are equally way too fanatic for my taste, then there was the Ordo Dracul. But then again, I thought, if you had to be like a Tzimisce obsess with transformation and shit, transcending and metamorphosis hell no. I thought, while my vampire could be interested in controlling the best and not being control by it, I can't imagine he would spend any significant amount of time joining an association bent on transcending.<br /> <br /> So maybe my character would be unaligned, but I was like, is unaligned not the new - Caitiff of Requiem, where everyone is suspicious and would prefer you dead than walking. (Pun intended)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the general idea here (and honestly the whole difference when coming from cWoD to nWod (CofD)) is that all of those things are just way more chill. The Covenents are not this super overbearing structural system, they are just some parts of the vampire society, use them as much or as little as you want in any given Chronicle. And the Clans being less politcally entites is this too, being a Venture doesn't define everything about you here, its just a description of your abilities and a bit where they come from (far less of a certain thing then the clans in Masquerade beyond your immediate sire and some close connections).<br /> <br /> Your character idea certainly sounds unaligned or maybe a few dots into Invictus or Carthian if you use your money and fame to sway politics at all. You can gain rank int he Status merit for things outside the Covenents too, like the city itself, plus there is Resources to show getting rich and Fame for famous-ness. Plus contacts, allies, retainers, and staff for other networking things that show your progression. Don't have to resrict youself so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:38:53-07:00","id":893676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893605#post893605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank I enjoyed reading your reply, it was indeed very concise and I think found a source of interest in, a sense I guess I prefer a more involve war between covenant or Sect of VTM over a less involve Sect of the VTR. Although now that many have explain, I didn't think many would just pay lip service to these sect, so now they may be more playable in my view, I thought that adhering to these sect meant like you had to work constantly toward the covenant goal, like what would happen if I was a Ventrue (Arm trafficker) think The Movie Lord of War (with Nicolas Cage) and I join the Carthian Movement because they offer sanctuary and protection, and Invictus system prevent me from increasing power, so I join them.<br /> <br /> But, as I become more powerful, and I reveal myself to be more of a Power freak, wanting to dominate and rule over other kindred, would I be killed by the covenant ?<br /> <br /> Then at that point would Invictus accepted me within their lot, if I am powerful enough. Or would they rally against me and destroy me and take what I have ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893611#post893611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b...</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for your answer I found them insightful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893636#post893636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThanks for replying, correcting some of my misconception from my read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893605#post893605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your reply I find it very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:46:37-07:00","id":893681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893675#post893675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the general idea here (and honestly the whole difference when coming from cWoD to nWod (CofD)) is that all of those things are just way more chill. The Covenents are not this super overbearing structural system, they are just some parts of the vampire society, use them as much or as little as you want in any given Chronicle. And the Clans being less politcally entites is this too, being a Venture doesn't define everything about you here, its just a description of your abilities and a bit where they come from (far less of a certain thing then the clans in Masquerade beyond your immediate sire and some close connections).<br /> <br /> Your character idea certainly sounds unaligned or maybe a few dots into Invictus or Carthian if you use your money and fame to sway politics at all. You can gain rank int he Status merit for things outside the Covenents too, like the city itself, plus there is Resources to show getting rich and Fame for famous-ness. Plus contacts, allies, retainers, and staff for other networking things that show your progression. Don't have to resrict youself so much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well I think that answered much of my problem right there, I didn't think the Covenant could be just have a little presence as you mention, having a mindset of VTM, I thought these organisation are like World wide monster infiltrated in most of the western world, something akin to the Camarilla but less powerful, but because its smaller it could manage to scrutinize its member that much more. I like the way you have put thing into perspective, they don't seem that bad anymore, and also if Unaligned doesn't necessarily put you into a hit list to be killed or destroy, it sounds more interesting to me a lot more now. Thank for the reply<br /> <br /> oh but if you don't mind sharing your thought on those question ;<br /> <br /> But, as I become more powerful, and I reveal myself to be more of a Power freak, wanting to dominate and rule over other kindred, would I be killed by the covenant ? (if I had join the Carthian Movement)<br /> <br /> Then at that point would Invictus accepted me within their lot, if I am powerful enough. Or would they rally against me and destroy me and take what I have ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:49:09-07:00","id":893683,"title":"","content":"I'm probably recapping a lot of things people have said earlier here (Atamajakki is right about the five covenants all, in some way, embodying way of dealing with becoming a vampire.) but first and foremost, as ElvesOfZion said, it's not really about better or worse. It's about difference. And difference and variety a big thing for the covenants of Requiem, especially, but not uniquely, In 2E. <br /> <br /> The Carthians are often firebrands opposing the status quo, but fundamentally they represent a challenge to the idea of elders ruling over younger vampires and accept that democracy has a place. They're also much more attuned to the modern world in many books/portrayals - part of the reason many Carthians opposed elder supremacy is, well, those guys can't use Google! In these days of catfishing. Ubers and other services, it's never been easier to get a meal without hitting the streets and leaving the safety of your haven - humans have so much to teach Kindred.<br /> The Movement grew from political experimentation, and this is still part of their ethos. They ape different human power structures, most importantly when they do run the show, which (as has been mentioned) can as varied as, say, a socialist commune or a neoconservative, Randian society focused on individualism, freedom and selfishness. The Carthians are occasionally also shown to be adapting the world to themselves. Did you think it was a coincidence that vampires have become sexy antiheroes and romantic leads in fiction rather than leering monsters? The Movement's been chipping away at the stone for some time (admittedly not solely). Heck, in <i>Danse Macabre </i>they were recast as wanting to eventually tear down the Masquerade (this is in no way canon, though with VtR's toolkit approach it could be), influencing human culture as mentioned and also having experimental villages where vampires lived openly,<br /> <br /> The Invictus are the status quo, but their system has stood the test of time for a reason. Elder rule the roost, sure, but the 1E sourcebook on them really explained how the Invictus society functions. The courtly ettiquette and political jockeying for power helps to keep elders grounded and lets vampires express their competitive, predatory urges without literally tearing one another apart. Why would younger vampire join them? The first reason is not just their wealth and influence, but a system of patronage. Sure, the elders run the show, but their favoured ancillae and neonates get access to their resources, their knowledge, their support and protection. Another huge part of the Invctus is that they, more than any other Covenant, are the conspiracy of silence. They're the Masquerade's fiercest defenders and many vampires are prepared to support, or fully sign up, for this alone.<br /> <br /> The Lancea are an interesting one. They're a Christian offshoot, not quite Catholic I'd argue (though variety within it relating to human subdivisions of Christianity never gets enough focus IMO) and they proclaim themselves holy predators,God's scourge against man. They're religiously empowered to be monsters! But with limits - they embody the 'Beast I am lest a Beast I become' more than any other Covenant. A good example is that the Lancea might spare good Christians, or might tempt them and punish them, like Job, to test their faith. They offer a reason and a place for vampires, and they don't want vampires to give in to the Beast. The most likely vampires to try to prevent you from becoming draugr are probably Santified. Also their Theban miracles can be convincing.That said, they're pretty happy to destroy anything that contradicts their official histories, especially in 2E. Something in 1e and 2e that's worth mentioning is that members of other Covenants may attend Midnight Mass and consider themselves Sanctified, though such dual-members are unlikely to be given any Theban lessons.<br /> <br /> The Circle, in both 1e and 2e, are incredibly diverse. They're inheritors of ancient traditons dating back thousands of years... and recent fads, all at once. The Crones in one city are likely to be entirely different to those in another, They share blood magic and a core belief that the vampire state isn't a curse, it's entirely natural and should be embraced (pun intended) and even shared, but not much else. I think the veneration of creation was played down a bit for 2e, though the vageuly matriarchal/strict gender roles is often ascribed to them to play up their pagan/witch sides, the diversity of different Crone cults makes even this far from a unifying concept. Their 'we're natural' pitch is a strong one too, though of course this can lead to them being far more accepting of Humanity loss...<br /> <br /> And the Dragons are pretty simple to grok, they're wanting to transcend their current state, with a mix of occultism and mad science. They also have a huge focus on evolving through struggle that makes them far more willing to endure burdens other vampires would consider insane, They like to experiment a lot, too, and they're sometimes prone to poking things just to see what happens. And, of course, the Coils strongly imply that their methodology works. <br /> <br /> Unaligned vampires are obviously individuals. I can see a lot of potential power for vampires who remain neutral, perhaps as arbiters, mercenaries, independent power-brokers the factions have to deal with, as well any non-joiners and Kindred 'losers'. There's always the potential for unaligned vampires to form local organisations, too - as has been mentioned, 2e provides examples of very local covenants that can be just as important, or more important, than any of the big five. There also places where the waters have muddied, occasionally even between the groups which seem the most obviously antagonistic (Circle/Lancea, Invictus/Carthian). . . <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:57:04-07:00","id":893693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893676#post893676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> like what would happen if I was a Ventrue (Arm trafficker) think The Movie Lord of War (with Nicolas Cage) and I join the Carthian Movement because they offer sanctuary and protection, and Invictus system prevent me from increasing power, so I join them.<br /> <br /> But, as I become more powerful, and I reveal myself to be more of a Power freak, wanting to dominate and rule over other kindred, would I be killed by the covenant ?<br /> <br /> Then at that point would Invictus accepted me within their lot, if I am powerful enough. Or would they rally against me and destroy me and take what I have ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend on how you go about it, I mean if you slowly build up a power base while providing aid to the carthian movement and then one day turn on them all and state they are now yours to control, then yeah there are probably some that will call for your head, from all the Kindred too, not just the carthians. Cause, that sounds like the thing a crazy super villain would do. But if you put some effort into getting more and more Kindred to agree that you should be in charge over time, and then make a coup, well if you win it then you win it, and now you are in charge of that chunk of territory (city most like but what ever you got).<br /> <br /> Other cities Invictus might respect your play for power and allow you to sign on, but maybe your followers wouldnt appreciate that since you found a way to make them follow you rather than the Invictus anyway. At this point you may just be an Invictus by another name.<br /> <br /> Really the point is, this isn't a video game. There is no set reaction that will happen. What happens is what you, the other players and Storyteller want to happen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:06:10-07:00","id":893698,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Defection</b><br /> <br /> In VTM, crossing the line from Camarilla to Sabbat was tantamount to suicide - only the strongest or most well connected even considered it and even then they would spend the rest of their unlives looking over their shoulders.<br /> <br /> In VTR, things are far more fluid and situational. There is no hard rule that says a vampire cannot jump from one covenant to another, and the fiction suggests this is not an uncommon practice, especially as the Vampire ages and their desires/motives change. However, expect bridges to be burned and feathers ruffled - most of the Covenants take a dim view of traitors (especially if there is a risk of mystic secrets being shared with the unworthy). Depending on the Vampires relationship to his Covenant and the exact circumstances of defection, it could be anything from a amicable split to a violent blood-vendetta.<br /> <br /> Having run both VTM and VTR extensively, the lack of monolithic world-spanning power blocks in VtR makes almost everything a bit more personal, which I consider a good thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:10:23-07:00","id":893701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893683#post893683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Unaligned vampires are obviously individuals. I can see a lot of potential power for vampires who remain neutral, perhaps as arbiters, mercenaries, independent power-brokers the factions have to deal with, as well any non-joiners and Kindred 'losers'. There's always the potential for unaligned vampires to form local organisations, too - as has been mentioned, 2e provides examples of very local covenants that can be just as important, or more important, than any of the big five. There also places where the waters have muddied, occasionally even between the groups which seem the most obviously antagonistic (Circle/Lancea, Invictus/Carthian). . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you it was an interesting read, In particular the last paragraph, very interesting that there could be other covenant, also that the covenant would see advantages in dealing with character that are neutral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893693#post893693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really the point is, this isn't a video game. There is no set reaction that will happen. What happens is what you, the other players and Storyteller want to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you again for your answer, and Good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893698#post893698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Defection</b><br /> <br /> In VTM, crossing the line from Camarilla to Sabbat was tantamount to suicide - only the strongest or most well connected even considered it and even then they would spend the rest of their unlives looking over their shoulders.<br /> <br /> In VTR, things are far more fluid and situational. There is no hard rule that says a vampire cannot jump from one covenant to another, and the fiction suggests this is not an uncommon practice, especially as the Vampire ages and their desires/motives change. However, expect bridges to be burned and feathers ruffled - most of the Covenants take a dim view of traitors (especially if there is a risk of mystic secrets being shared with the unworthy). Depending on the Vampires relationship to his Covenant and the exact circumstances of defection, it could be anything from a amicable split to a violent blood-vendetta.<br /> <br /> Having run both VTM and VTR extensively, the lack of monolithic world-spanning power blocks in VtR makes almost everything a bit more personal, which I consider a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I guess that another point I was wondering about, and your answer - answering pretty much my concern about my other post about leaving the Carthian movement to become Invictus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:12:28-07:00","id":893704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893698#post893698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Defection</b><br /> <br /> In VTM, crossing the line from Camarilla to Sabbat was tantamount to suicide - only the strongest or most well connected even considered it and even then they would spend the rest of their unlives looking over their shoulders.<br /> <br /> In VTR, things are far more fluid and situational. There is no hard rule that says a vampire cannot jump from one covenant to another, and the fiction suggests this is not an uncommon practice, especially as the Vampire ages and their desires/motives change. However, expect bridges to be burned and feathers ruffled - most of the Covenants take a dim view of traitors (especially if there is a risk of mystic secrets being shared with the unworthy). Depending on the Vampires relationship to his Covenant and the exact circumstances of defection, it could be anything from a amicable split to a violent blood-vendetta.<br /> <br /> Having run both VTM and VTR extensively, the lack of monolithic world-spanning power blocks in VtR makes almost everything a bit more personal, which I consider a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And to re-iterate what i said in my first (adimattidly big) post, in 2nd edition you can explicitly have Status in more than one Covenent (albit with some restriction).<br /> <br /> It is also mentioned that you can follow the others as parts of life without really being a member. For instance, in many cities the Invictus and Lance have a pretty tight relationship, one being governmental and the other spiritual. Members of the Invictus are generally expected to attend Lance ceremonies as lay-persons semi regularly in this case. Other simialr relationships can exist thought the world with other covenant groupings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:17:36-07:00","id":893710,"title":"","content":"Those aren't questions that have single answers. As you noted, the intent of the Covenants by default is to be &quot;smaller&quot; and more &quot;local&quot; than the VtM Sects.<br /> <br /> While the major Covenants of Requiem are large spread philosophies, they are are varied as human philosophies. Just as Christianity is not the same everywhere you go, the Lancea et Sanctum is not the same everywhere you go. Local politics, customs, and culture matter more than what some other member of the Covenant is doing half a world away.<br /> <br /> One city's Carthians might seek the destruction of a vampire seeking ultimate power over all other Kindred, while those in another might not care in the slightest as long as said vampire plays by the rules. If your lust for power can be sated without violating the laws of the undead, then you earned it.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Invictus are not a monolith where all of them have a single opinion about an upstart power hungry non-Invictus vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:31:43-07:00","id":893720,"title":"","content":"Is the Ordo Dracul the continuation of the Path of Metamorphosis from VTM, are you expected to mold your skin and change your appearance to something terrifying. (Not that the Tzimisce could mold themselves into a perfect human body but it always seem to me that the setting was more about the Tzimisce becoming monster and accepting that they are no longer human but a monster and embracing all of it to become a true horror.<br /> <br /> I would be looking more for something like The Path of Entelechy - From Lore of the Clan V20 page 51-52. Its closely tie to humanity but concentrate on not acting on impulse or losing yourself to the beast and having high willpower or pursuing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:36:28-07:00","id":893723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893704#post893704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And to re-iterate what i said in my first (adimattidly big) post, in 2nd edition you can explicitly have Status in more than one Covenent (albit with some restriction).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I read that the first time , but didn't pay to much attention to it, but ok, so if I was to have Status with say, The Invictus and Ordo Dracul or Invictus and Carthian Movement, it doesn't make me part of them does it, its just that I have attain some form of respect with both covenant that is correct no ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:47:31-07:00","id":893728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893710#post893710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those aren't questions that have single answers. As you noted, the intent of the Covenants by default is to be &quot;smaller&quot; and more &quot;local&quot; than the VtM Sects.<br /> <br /> While the major Covenants of Requiem are large spread philosophies, they are are varied as human philosophies. Just as Christianity is not the same everywhere you go, the Lancea et Sanctum is not the same everywhere you go. Local politics, customs, and culture matter more than what some other member of the Covenant is doing half a world away.<br /> <br /> One city's Carthians might seek the destruction of a vampire seeking ultimate power over all other Kindred, while those in another might not care in the slightest as long as said vampire plays by the rules. If your lust for power can be sated without violating the laws of the undead, then you earned it.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Invictus are not a monolith where all of them have a single opinion about an upstart power hungry non-Invictus vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So do you usually have different, diverging version of 1 sect from city to city, or is it just something hinted at in the book but less of a thing in game, it is common for VTR game to have like a vampire from Say Crone to be unwelcome in another city because of them being more extremist in another city. Or not have the same festival , or not being accepted because said person does not recognize the deity the others venerate in this city, so they are unwelcome ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:26:46-07:00","id":893741,"title":"","content":"The thing you have to understand about Vampire the Requiem is that everything - <i>everything</i> - is trends and generalities. Just like in real life, you can't say that anything is unilaterally true about a group of people (or in this case, a group of vampires). All you can talk about is how this group holds these ideals, or that group encourages that behavior, or members of this group are often like this. There will always be individual exceptions to everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893720#post893720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Ordo Dracul the continuation of the Path of Metamorphosis from VTM, are you expected to mold your skin and change your appearance to something terrifying. (Not that the Tzimisce could mold themselves into a perfect human body but it always seem to me that the setting was more about the Tzimisce becoming monster and accepting that they are no longer human but a monster and embracing all of it to become a true horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The Ordo Dracul are interested in transcending the limitations of the vampiric condition, while taking full advantage of its strengths. There's nothing about their philosophy that requires body modification of any kind, let alone modification with the specific intent of becoming more monstrous or horrifying. Some might go about it that way, but there are plenty of others who go about trying to improve themselves in other ways. The Ordo Dracul doesn't much care about how you go about trying to transcend the curse - body modification, performance enhancers, psychoactive drugs, meditation, whatever floats your boat. It's all very personal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893720#post893720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be looking more for something like The Path of Entelechy - From Lore of the Clan V20 page 51-52. Its closely tie to humanity but concentrate on not acting on impulse or losing yourself to the beast and having high willpower or pursuing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That mindset could fit pretty well into the Ordo Dracul. It could probably also fit into any Covenant, honestly, but if you're trying to better yourself though these self-control exercises (for example, to learn to better control yourself when you Frenzy), that would absolutely be something the Ordo Dracul would approve of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893723#post893723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I read that the first time , but didn't pay to much attention to it, but ok, so if I was to have Status with say, The Invictus and Ordo Dracul or Invictus and Carthian Movement, it doesn't make me part of them does it, its just that I have attain some form of respect with both covenant that is correct no ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Covenant Status represents actual membership in the Covenant, and usually higher Status comes with more responsibilities, as well as greater influence. The rule in 2nd edition is that you can have Status in multiple Covenants, as long as your total Covenant Status isn't greater than 5, and your &quot;primary&quot; Covenant has the most dots. This basically represents the fact that the more influential you are in any Covenant, the less likely other Covenants are going to be to trust you in important roles within their organization. So you can dedicate yourself fully to one Covenant, or you can become a mid-ranking member of two, or you can become a lower-ranking member of three or four. Normally, you can't be a member of all five, but there is also a Carthian-only Merit that lets you ignore your Carthian Status for these purposes, so theoretically a Carthian could have a little bit of influence in every Covenant and still be an important figure within the Movement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893728#post893728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do you usually have different, diverging version of 1 sect from city to city, or is it just something hinted at in the book but less of a thing in game, it is common for VTR game to have like a vampire from Say Crone to be unwelcome in another city because of them being more extremist in another city. Or not have the same festival , or not being accepted because said person does not recognize the deity the others venerate in this city, so they are unwelcome ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that kind of thing is fairly common. It goes back to the thing I said in the beginning of this post about generalities. In some cities, the Circle of the Crone might have more stringent regulations than others. They might hold different festivals or venerate different Gods. In one city, they might be outlawed as a heretical faction of witches, while in another they might be valued advisors to the Prince in spiritual matters. The same goes for all of the Covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:27:48-07:00","id":893743,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: The Ordo</b><br /> <br /> Think of the Dragons as a direct analog to the Path of Metamorphosis. However, the Dragons differ in that they (generally) do not get hung up on physically expressing their inhuman nature. A Dragon would likely consider the Path of Metamorphosis an interesting, but somewhat crude approach to Transcendence. The Dragons seek to overcome the limitations imposed by the Curse of Vampirism. Once this is done, they will become something as far beyond vampire as Vampire is above Man.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Dual Membership</b><br /> <br /> By the rules, this is possibly, but will be heavily dependent on the campaign. Certain covenants are philosophically opposed enough that having status in both is unlikely ( Invictus/Carthian, Lancea/Crone) but stranger things have happened. Typically speaking, One covenant would take precedence over the other. In a domain where the Invictus and the Ordo share resources, A Status 3 Dragon might also hold Status 1 in the Invictus with no conflict of interest.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Local Changes</b><br /> <br /> They type of reception a Vampire receives when meeting up with covenant members in a different Domain is going to be based entirely on the domains in question (and more importantly, the Storyteller in question). The rules assume that each domain will be familiar enough to recognize the Covenants for what they are, but different enough that you can't take anything for granted. a Crone from a domain where the Crone are in charge is going to be in for a shock if they travel to a domain where the Crone are on the defensive.<br /> VTM was built heavily on stereotypes and had organizations with ideology that was very consistent on a global level. In VTR there are basic expectations, but the details can shift from domain to domain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:54:11-07:00","id":893755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893741#post893741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you all your answers were very insightful about the game, and its covenants. <br /> <br /> I can appreciate what they went for a bit more, it's about giving more leeway for the storyteller about what these covenant can be within your story, VTR gives you a general idea but they can be anything that fit their ideals. They can be as present or absent that fits the mood of your game. Although after everything said, I am having difficulty imagining different version of the Invictus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893743#post893743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: The Ordo</b><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Local Changes</b><br /> <br /> They type of reception a Vampire receives when meeting up with covenant members in a different Domain is going to be based entirely on the domains in question (and more importantly, the Storyteller in question). The rules assume that each domain will be familiar enough to recognize the Covenants for what they are, but different enough that you can't take anything for granted. a Crone from a domain where the Crone are in charge is going to be in for a shock if they travel to a domain where the Crone are on the defensive.<br /> VTM was built heavily on stereotypes and had organizations with ideology that was very consistent on a global level. In VTR there are basic expectations, but the details can shift from domain to domain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you again for your input<br /> <br /> <br /> How would a domain control by Invictus differ from another domain control with Invictus ? and so If I understand properly covenant are usually only as large a a domain, and don't really stretch across multiple city if they have different prince. The invictus from Chicago don't have to answer to the Invictus of New York of Vice versa ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:33:10-07:00","id":893772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893755#post893755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can appreciate what they went for a bit more, it's about giving more leeway for the storyteller about what these covenant can be within your story, VTR gives you a general idea but they can be anything that fit their ideals. They can be as present or absent that fits the mood of your game. Although after everything said, I am having difficulty imagining different version of the Invictus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend taking a look at VtR 2e. It presents a much better take on the Invictus - as has been mentioned before, the stigma against new technology is no longer a thing, and have a much clearer and tighter focus. Finally, it has a lot of fantastic example domains, which do a great job of showing variation in how the Covenants behave from one domain to the next.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893755#post893755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a domain control by Invictus differ from another domain control with Invictus ? and so If I understand properly covenant are usually only as large a a domain, and don't really stretch across multiple city if they have different prince. The invictus from Chicago don't have to answer to the Invictus of New York of Vice versa ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Covenants are generally pretty locally run. There is communication between different domains (we live in the information age after all), but there aren't overarching power structures where the local Sheriff has to answer to the regional Judex or whatever. As for the Invictus specificaly, they have been re-focused a bit in Second Edition. Rather than being &quot;The Aristocracy of the Night&quot;, they've been re-branded as &quot;The Conspiracy of Silence&quot;. Rather than being all about neo-feudalism and maintaining the old ways, the Invictus of Second Edition are the self-styled enforcers of the Masquerade. They manipulate and control mortal power structures to put themselves into positions where they can make sure the people who see too much &quot;forget&quot; what they've seen, and the people who speak too much are discretely &quot;dealt with&quot;. They much more closely resemble the vampire mafia than the vampire... uhh... neo-feudal guys...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T18:42:21-07:00","id":893778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893772#post893772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would recommend taking a look at VtR 2e. It presents a much better take on the Invictus - as has been mentioned before, the stigma against new technology is no longer a thing, and have a much clearer and tighter focus. Finally, it has a lot of fantastic example domains, which do a great job of showing variation in how the Covenants behave from one domain to the next.<br /> <br /> <br /> Correct. Covenants are generally pretty locally run. There is communication between different domains (we live in the information age after all), but there aren't overarching power structures where the local Sheriff has to answer to the regional Judex or whatever. As for the Invictus specificaly, they have been re-focused a bit in Second Edition. Rather than being &quot;The Aristocracy of the Night&quot;, they've been re-branded as &quot;The Conspiracy of Silence&quot;. Rather than being all about neo-feudalism and maintaining the old ways, the Invictus of Second Edition are the self-styled enforcers of the Masquerade. They manipulate and control mortal power structures to put themselves into positions where they can make sure the people who see too much &quot;forget&quot; what they've seen, and the people who speak too much are discretely &quot;dealt with&quot;. They much more closely resemble the vampire mafia than the vampire... uhh... neo-feudal guys...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for taking time to explain this to me, I really appreciate it, and I am going to take your advice and try to get my hands on that 2nd edition, curious to read more about the game now, thank you to all again.<br /> <br /> Good evening to all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:05:06-07:00","id":893786,"title":"","content":"One thing I wanna toss out, since it doesn't seem to have come up, is that the contention between Covenants has dimmed down between Editions. As an example, the Carthians still casually point at the Invictus as their main example of why vampire society needs to change, but they also tend to appreciate that the system does neatly direct the Kindred condition into a stable community, and while the Invictus still see the Carthians as trying to fix a system that isn't broken, they do applaud the ways they've found to reinforce the standards of society effectively and quickly. In some cites, the old rivalry stands and they glare at each other from across the dinner table, but in other cities they work tightly together to create an thoroughly efficient, if at times brutal, vampire society, thick as thieves and reaping the benefits.<br /> <br /> In Masquerade, the factions were much more fixed in their issues with one another, be they Sects or Clans. In Requiem, every city plays out a little differently, and more often than not, the Covenants actually do work together just as much as they backstab each other, using their silk gloves and iron gauntlets in equal measure with one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T20:35:43-07:00","id":893836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893755#post893755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a domain control by Invictus differ from another domain control with Invictus ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for example the region of my game, I have the Invictus allies of all of the covenants and many other supernaturals, since they focus their efforts on just maintaining the masquerade and helping contact between the different supernaturals. They have a structure, but it's just &quot;Guys who have a lot of contacts, info, and preparation skills&quot; above &quot;invictis with a decent number of contacts or with dominate dots&quot; above &quot;other invictis&quot; They know what's going down, they modify peoples memories to maintain the masquerade, but they don't try to dominate the region, they just do communication and damage control so well that all the other covenants know that to be enemies with them would only harm themselves.<br /> <br /> The fact that you can have a covenant that is allied with all the others is something I rather like in Requiem. It's rather mutable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-20-2016, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T02:05:09-07:00","id":893910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893755#post893755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a domain control by Invictus differ from another domain control with Invictus?</div> </div> </div> </div>One Invictus domain may run like a classic noble court, with Prince as master of life and death and a strict hierarchy determining how deep you bow to whom.<br /> <br /> Another may run like a modern corporation, with elders as the board of directors and the Prince as CEO, where etiquette is not that strict and younger Kindred can mostly do whatever they want as long as they produce expected results.<br /> <br /> Another may run like Hellfire Club, where successful Kindred are tempted to join with all kinds of vices, pooling their resources when necessary to rule the city from shadows. In this case, everyone is a frenemy, <i>quid pro quo</i> is the whole of the law, and the oaths are taken in debauched mockery of old rituals, but are no less potent for it.<br /> <br /> That's just off the top of my head, and not taking into account how Invictus (or any other covenant, for that matter) can and will adapt to the influence of other covenants and their local idiosyncrasies. A domain where Invictus is allied with LetS will look different from one where it's in cahoots with the Dragons and opposed by Sanctified hardliners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and so If I understand properly covenant are usually only as large a a domain, and don't really stretch across multiple city if they have different prince. The invictus from Chicago don't have to answer to the Invictus of New York of Vice versa ? </div> </div> </div>By default, this is the case. It seems less set in stone in 2e, and some of the sample domains in 2e core show hints of how neighboring cities may influence each other, but your Invictus Prince of New York won't have to send reports to the King of America, and he may or may not have established relations with the Prince of Chicago, depending on the needs of your chronicle. Generally, the closer the two cities, and the more their IRL histories are intertwined, the bigger the chance of them having some relations and exchange, but the final decision is up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T09:32:07-07:00","id":894092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893675#post893675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the general idea here (and honestly the whole difference when coming from cWoD to nWod (CofD)) is that all of those things are just way more chill. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't let The Mother's Army hear you say that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:22:08-07:00","id":894142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=894092#post894092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't let The Mother's Army hear you say that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, well, 'in world' is a whole nother story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:27:54-07:00","id":894403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893786#post893786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I wanna toss out, since it doesn't seem to have come up, is that the contention between Covenants has dimmed down between Editions. As an example, the Carthians still casually point at the Invictus as their main example of why vampire society needs to change, but they also tend to appreciate that the system does neatly direct the Kindred condition into a stable community, and while the Invictus still see the Carthians as trying to fix a system that isn't broken, they do applaud the ways they've found to reinforce the standards of society effectively and quickly. In some cites, the old rivalry stands and they glare at each other from across the dinner table, but in other cities they work tightly together to create an thoroughly efficient, if at times brutal, vampire society, thick as thieves and reaping the benefits.<br /> <br /> In Masquerade, the factions were much more fixed in their issues with one another, be they Sects or Clans. In Requiem, every city plays out a little differently, and more often than not, the Covenants actually do work together just as much as they backstab each other, using their silk gloves and iron gauntlets in equal measure with one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically its very common for multiple sect to coexist within one city without thing turning into a blood bath - with one sect wiping out the other. Interesting definitely not something that would ever happen in VTM. _ Maybe the Camarilla and the Anarch but yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:34:45-07:00","id":894408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893910#post893910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Invictus domain may run like a classic noble court, with Prince as master of life and death and a strict hierarchy determining how deep you bow to whom.<br /> <br /> Another may run like a modern corporation, with elders as the board of directors and the Prince as CEO, where etiquette is not that strict and younger Kindred can mostly do whatever they want as long as they produce expected results.<br /> <br /> Another may run like Hellfire Club, where successful Kindred are tempted to join with all kinds of vices, pooling their resources when necessary to rule the city from shadows. In this case, everyone is a frenemy, <i>quid pro quo</i> is the whole of the law, and the oaths are taken in debauched mockery of old rituals, but are no less potent for it.<br /> <br /> That's just off the top of my head, and not taking into account how Invictus (or any other covenant, for that matter) can and will adapt to the influence of other covenants and their local idiosyncrasies. A domain where Invictus is allied with LetS will look different from one where it's in cahoots with the Dragons and opposed by Sanctified hardliners.<br /> <br /> <br /> By default, this is the case. It seems less set in stone in 2e, and some of the sample domains in 2e core show hints of how neighboring cities may influence each other, but your Invictus Prince of New York won't have to send reports to the King of America, and he may or may not have established relations with the Prince of Chicago, depending on the needs of your chronicle. Generally, the closer the two cities, and the more their IRL histories are intertwined, the bigger the chance of them having some relations and exchange, but the final decision is up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, ok its really weird, its so different from VTM, not sure If I prefer it or not, but I am diffinetely more curious about it, haven't started reading the 2e Edition yet, I will start reading it maybe later tonight or tomorrow. Thank for these example, they were interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893836#post893836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for example the region of my game, I have the Invictus allies of all of the clans and many other supernaturals, since they focus their efforts on just maintaining the masquerade and helping contact between the different supernaturals. They have a structure, but it's just &quot;Guys who have a lot of contacts, info, and preparation skills&quot; above &quot;invictis with a decent number of contacts or with dominate dots&quot; above &quot;other invictis&quot; They know what's going down, they modify peoples memories to maintain the masquerade, but they don't try to dominate the region, they just do communication and damage control so well that all the other covenants know that to be enemies with them would only harm themselves.<br /> <br /> The fact that you can have a covenant that is allied with all the others is something I rather like in Requiem. It's rather mutable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for sharing some experience, help me get a better picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1326-arcaneumkiller","name":"Arcaneumkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:38:38-07:00","id":894412,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I kind of took that as a given, since inter-Covenabt politicking is a huge part of Requiem. The vast majority of cities are multi-Covenant, and many, if not most, have all five spoken for. If animosity exists between them, it's usually the subtle, backstabby kind, not the all-out-war kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T05:29:40-07:00","id":894668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893786#post893786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I wanna toss out, since it doesn't seem to have come up, is that the contention between Covenants has dimmed down between Editions.</div> </div> </div> </div> To build on this - the 2e covenants were designed in such a way that each has a reason to keep the others around. The Invictus might not agree with the Carthians, but the Invictus Prince would look at Carthians and their ability to uphold city law as well as ignore treasonous compulsions, and actively recruit Carthians because of that. The Lance's magic is more judgemental and suited for hunting down, while the Crone's magic allows for more general divinations and insights - both are highly useful in their own ways. The Ordo can walk in the sunlight and inflict Vincs with ease, making them highly versatile.<br /> <br /> The five covenants not only are more cordial, but they also have reasons to actually want to work together and have a stronger, more stable city because of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:14:22-07:00","id":894728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=894408#post894408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm, ok its really weird, its so different from VTM, not sure If I prefer it or not, but I am diffinetely more curious about it, haven't started reading the 2e Edition yet, I will start reading it maybe later tonight or tomorrow. Thank for these example, they were interesting.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, the Covenants are really closer to VtM's Clan politics then the Sects. You can have them in a city working together or there can be animosity, all depends on the locale and the Kindred involved. Also, why the Clans feel anemic to you.<br /> <br /> To sum up:<br /> The covenants don't replace the Sects, the Sects just don't exist; the Covenents replace the political portion of the Clans, and the Clans just indicated some lineage based power set stuff. There are also Bloodlines, which do bring some of the politics back sometimes but not nessacrily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:40:13-07:00","id":894743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=894728#post894728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, the Covenants are really closer to VtM's Clan politics then the Sects. You can have them in a city working together or there can be animosity, all depends on the locale and the Kindred involved. Also, why the Clans feel anemic to you.<br /> <br /> To sum up:<br /> The covenants don't replace the Sects, the Sects just don't exist; the Covenents replace the political portion of the Clans, and the Clans just indicated some lineage based power set stuff. There are also Bloodlines, which do bring some of the politics back sometimes but not nessacrily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T08:50:59-07:00","id":894747,"title":"","content":"Totalitarian strongman ruling over a workers paradise is as valid a Carthian setup as open, unlimited democracy. Ones just a lot darker than the other, and an example of the Carthians gone wrong.<br /> <br /> All you have to do is convince the rest of the Carthians is that you are ushering in a new age of sisterhood that will treat everyone fairly and that only way to do so is to give you complete control over everything. You will selflessly administer this mess for the betterment of all.<br /> <br /> All the Covenants have better and worse sides.<br /> <br /> As for being killed, that depends on a lot of items (murdering other vamps is usually illegal, but not always in every city). All it takes is one angry kindred with a stake....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:05:50-07:00","id":895222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=894728#post894728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I said, the Covenants are really closer to VtM's Clan politics then the Sects. You can have them in a city working together or there can be animosity, all depends on the locale and the Kindred involved. Also, why the Clans feel anemic to you.<br /> <br /> To sum up:<br /> The covenants don't replace the Sects, the Sects just don't exist; the Covenents replace the political portion of the Clans, and the Clans just indicated some lineage based power set stuff. There are also Bloodlines, which do bring some of the politics back sometimes but not nessacrily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nailed it. Clan identity barely exists in VtR, with Covenants filling that void; the Sects gave no real equivalent, and the game is better for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-23-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T09:57:59-07:00","id":895532,"title":"","content":"Well, there is the Strix...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T16:37:40-07:00","id":896382,"title":"","content":"Yep the covenants are not the new sects. They are the new clans. For example there is always a conservative group and a progressive group in a wod game. In Masquerade the Ventrue clan was the conservative group (doing things the way it's been done for centuries) and the Brujah clan was the progressive group looking for a way to change the system. Just like the Invictus and the Carthians in Requiem. It's all pretty political with all factions having their own ideology crafted. Big tricky part is always the question &quot;What do they do?&quot;, because they aren't really geared towards having practical goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:48:36-07:00","id":896851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=895222#post895222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nailed it. Clan identity barely exists in VtM, with Covenants filling that void; the Sects gave no real equivalent, and the game is better for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you meant VtR. Only matters for someone who might read it and be confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:44:22-07:00","id":896939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=896851#post896851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think you meant VtR. Only matters for someone who might read it and be confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:54:33-07:00","id":897225,"title":"","content":"Aye, in VtM, Clan was both &quot;What you are&quot; and &quot;What do you do&quot;. In VtR, Clan is &quot;What you are&quot; and Covenant is &quot;What you do&quot;. When 1e first came out, Clan still had a minor political role (look at the 1st edition main book, and it's references to clan primogen and whips), versus 2e, which only really has Clan Status, and other familial relations in politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:38:59-07:00","id":897748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=897225#post897225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When 1e first came out, Clan still had a minor political role (look at the 1st edition main book, and it's references to clan primogen and whips)(...)</div> </div> </div> </div>1e had quite a few holdovers from Masquerade. I even recall a couple paragraphs in the core that I could swear were straight-up copied from VtM Revised core.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:30:48-07:00","id":897782,"title":"","content":"I always saw clan as entity as mentioned in 1st edition core, then downplayed to nothing and then reinforced really strong towards the end of the run of 1st ed. The clanbooks emphasize clan as a community like nothing else in the run did. You know, Nosferatu necropolis, coteries of Gangrel etc.<br /> <br /> I don't think its been downplayed all that much between 1st and 2nd. In 1st ed core you had Clan Status, Whips and Priscus. There was no mention of Primogen being clan specific. Since 2nd ed only really mentions Prince, Primogen and Harpies, I don't necessarily see it as a big change in focus from 1st ed, Also, Damnation City is mentioned as an applicable book in the introduction chapter of 2nd and that one calls out Prisci explicitly. Oddly enough, its mostly the clan books in that section and those push clan as a community/organization more than any other book in the line.<br /> <br /> I personally like the pulls of &quot;family&quot; in a game. Less powerful/official than Covenant, but its still there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:49:14-07:00","id":900022,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla and Invictus are pretty much pallete-swaps of each other, both meritocracies were the merit is age, though that does work slightly less well in Requiem, what with the way Blood Potency works. Still, the Invictus and Camarilla are both stultifying pyramid-scheme power structures with little room for advancement for the neonate.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat from Masquerade was intended by a pure villain faction, until people decided they liked them better than the Camarilla, they underwent serious villain decay, and became a playable faction. This really damaged some of the core concepts of the Sabbat, notably not giving a crap about the Masquerade became a lip-service philosophy, with them still hiding from mortals most of the time, and in the end pretty much made the Sabbat just the Camarilla with a different set of titles and a <i>slightly</i> less draconian policy on diablerie. The Sabbat have kind of been split in three, depending on how you want to look at it: Part of them is the Lancea Sanctum, with the religious overtones (also toned down a lot as the Sabbat underwent villain decay), part of them is the Carthian Movment, and the implacable, unknowable villain faction is VII.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs become the other half of the Carthian Movement, the ones who want change, violently if necessary (sometimes if not).<br /> <br /> The Inconnu are gone, and I rather say good riddance. They were pretty much just mysterious for mysterious sake. Joining the Inconnu was pretty much just another nonstandard game over, as your character retreats to whatever mystic temple they're holing themselves up in and spends the rest of eternity contemplating their navel.<br /> <br /> As for the Requiem Covenants, while a number of them borrow themes from some of the earlier Sects, they're still very much their own animals. The Invictus are the closest to a direct import, being more or less Requiem's Camarilla (though the Camarilla did exist in Requiem, in Ancient Rome, and it didn't fare well). The Carthians are kind of the Anarchs with some Sabbat thrown in, the Lancea Sanctum have a Sabbat veneer but with a wholly different motivation, and the Circle and Ordo are pretty much completely new.<br /> <br /> The main advantage to the new Covenants is that they're frameworks on which to build. In Masquerade, the Camarilla was the Camarilla no matter where you went, it was a world-wide organization. In any Camarilla city, the same basic laws were in play, with only minor variations based on the whim of that particular prince. The Sabbat was also pretty much the same wherever you went. In Requiem, while the Invictus is an old, tradition-bound Covenant, exactly what that means to the Covenant in any given city can be wildly different. One city could operate exactly like a Game of Thrones-esque medieval court, another might be a pre-revolutionary aristocracy, yet another might be parliament council with members chosen from a &quot;nobility&quot; of some kind. Heck, the Invictus in one my cities in my on-hold game is a Mafia family. The Carthians may be true anarchs, set only on disrupting whatever status quo currently exists, they may be true &quot;power to the people&quot; democrats, absolute Marxist communists, or supporting &quot;the Glorious Democratic People's Republic Of South Gothtropolis And Its Beloved President For Unlife.&quot; The Circle can be harmless hippy-dippy spiritualists, hardcore human-sacrificing evil witches, scary powerful neutral witches who's bad sides you don't want to get on, or mysterious wise women. The Sanctum can be a full-tilt religion of evil, a misguided and corrupt church, or an institution desperately trying to provide some meaning and guidance to the unlives of the Kindred. The Ordo Dracul can be crazy philosophers, vile mad scientists, despicable Nietzsche wannabes, or erudite scholars who understand the ins and outs of the vampiric condition. It's all about how you want to play any or all of them in your game. Requiem is a sandbox game, and the tools are there for individual storytellers and players to make use of. No one vision of any of the Covenants is any more correct than the others, and that's what makes them better than the Sects of Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:52:28-07:00","id":900091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=900022#post900022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Requiem Covenants, while a number of them borrow themes from some of the earlier Sects, they're still very much their own animals. The Invictus are the closest to a direct import, being more or less Requiem's Camarilla (though the Camarilla did exist in Requiem, in Ancient Rome, and it didn't fare well). The Carthians are kind of the Anarchs with some Sabbat thrown in, the Lancea Sanctum have a Sabbat veneer but with a wholly different motivation, and the Circle and Ordo are pretty much completely new.</div> </div> </div> </div>The circle and Ordo are not wholly new at all. The circle is philosophicly almost identical to the Sabbath and the Ordo is the path of metamorphosis stripped of the flesh crafting and with occults bell and whistle added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:14:09-07:00","id":900244,"title":"","content":"I originally thought the circle had some tie ins to the old path of lilith. Its less of that now, but when originally described in a spoiler, that where my head went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:25:46-07:00","id":900248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=900091#post900091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The circle is philosophicly almost identical to the Sabbath</div> </div> </div> </div>Presuming you mean the Sabbat, this is incorrect. The Sabbat are a political party, and thus focused externally. They believe, foremost, in loyalty to their superiors and coterie-mates, freedom to live without being unfairly manipulated by elders, and war. The Circle of the Crone are a philosophy, they believe the Beast is a gift, the Vampire is a natural part of the world, and in appreciating Humanity even as you shed it to become something greater, specifically, closer to your Beast. If you wanted to say the Circle was like something in Masquerade it should be the Path of the Beast, but even that doesn't fit due to the changed nature of the Beast and the concepts of creation and naturalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:26:09-07:00","id":900355,"title":"","content":"I find it rather confusing that so many people are quick to associate the Ordo with the Path of Metaphoresis, but miss out on the Inconnu, Tremere and a few other influences. While I don't think anyone is going to argue that the covenants weren't inspired by parts of Masquerade, its not a simple 1-for-1 correspondance here, and the covenants have grown in different ways beyond their original roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:55:53-07:00","id":900386,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The Path of Metamorphosis is about change, but they go about it in drastically different ways. The Path are solitary scientists, who refuse to share their information. They believe there is no one way to master change and that everyone has to try changing themselves as much as possible. Their goals are different, as well, with the Path seeking out mostly physical and spiritual might, and not the sort of overcoming of weaknesses and embracing of powers that the Ordo is into. As their name suggests, the Path promotes change simply for changes sake, anything that might get you an edge, while the Ordo believe change without purpose is pointless. Followers of the Path believe humans are completely unworthy of notice, while the Ordo believes them to be premier examples of change, as they are not 'static' like most of the dead. They're both about change, but they go about it in different ways, their aims are different, and Ordo experimentation results in Coils and Scales.<br /> <br /> And the Path of Metamorphosis is just as laden with occult bells and whistles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-26-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:37:44-07:00","id":902566,"title":"","content":"Re the Camarilla and Invictus:<br /> <br /> I actually view them as inversions, rather than copies, of each other.<br /> <br /> Elders in the Camarilla want to accrue power, and they use the Masquerade to do it. They pretend to care about the Masquerade, so they &quot;have to&quot; create rules and a hierarchy and keep the neonates/ancillae in line, but really they just want to sit at the top of the food chain and grow fat.<br /> <br /> The Invictus, however, wants to protect the secret (ie keep the Masquerade) and uses power to do that. After all, it's a lot easier to maintain the Masquerade if you carry a big stick to keep your fellow vampires in line, can discretely get mortal journalists reassigned as needed, etc. This also accounts for their newfound tech savvy (compared to 1E): they're on an all-night alert that lets them know when they need to step in.<br /> <br /> So they look the same on the outside, but dig deeper and they're really not.<br /> <br /> Edit to clarify: I'm going off VtR 2E","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":1713,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","user":"mistress of whispers","date":". 05-29-2016, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T02:34:55-07:00","id":902587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=900248#post900248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presuming you mean the Sabbat, this is incorrect. The Sabbat are a political party, and thus focused externally. They believe, foremost, in loyalty to their superiors and coterie-mates, freedom to live without being unfairly manipulated by elders, and war. The Circle of the Crone are a philosophy, they believe the Beast is a gift, the Vampire is a natural part of the world, and in appreciating Humanity even as you shed it to become something greater, specifically, closer to your Beast. If you wanted to say the Circle was like something in Masquerade it should be the Path of the Beast, but even that doesn't fit due to the changed nature of the Beast and the concepts of creation and naturalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the book have to say about the Sabbat, you're mistaking the trappings for the actual substance of the things.<br /> <br /> Here is what the 20th anniversary book has to say about the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the \u201cKindred\u201d (a term the Sabbat despise) of the Ivory Tower cower among mortals and cling to outdated Traditions, <b>the Sabbat prefer to indulge in their vampiric nature.</b> </div> </div> </div>This the core of Sabbat philosophy, they aren't human and won't act like them. This is the part that inspired the circle of the crone. I never said the circle was a carbon copy of the Sabbat, just that it didn't come out of nowhere, there always was a faction whose motto was &quot;we are monsters and we'll act like one&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:24:56-07:00","id":902794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=902587#post902587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what the book have to say about the Sabbat, you're mistaking the trappings for the actual substance of the things.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could say you're taking one line out of context and placing too much importance on it. The actual substance of things matter than one hyperbolic line that doesn't even scratch the surface of the sect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here is what the 20th anniversary book has to say about the Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>It's followed by pages explaining the depth of their differences with the Circle of the Crone, as well as establishing their preeminent political beliefs outlined in the Code of Milan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This the core of Sabbat philosophy, they aren't human and won't act like them. This is the part that inspired the circle of the crone. I never said the circle was a carbon copy of the Sabbat, just that it didn't come out of nowhere, there always was a faction whose motto was &quot;we are monsters and we'll act like one&quot; </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=900091#post900091\">You said that their philosophy was almost identical</a>, that is what I responded to. Regardless, that's not the Circle motto. The motto is more like, 'We're vampires and that's alright.' It doesn't support viewing humanity as food or tools or even viewing themselves as alien. This is why I tried to explain the Circle to you, so you would understand that they are not just about acting like monsters. And frankly, it's not even the Sabbat motto, This is why the Sabbat section has two more pages detailing how they're not just 'monsters acting like monsters,' even pointing out that they follow Paths in order to curb their gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Masquerade 20th Anniversary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They adhere to a wide variety of Paths of Enlightenment, philosophical tenets that force the Beast into a narrow channel and allow the Cainite to maintain a day-to-day existence that resembles stability (if not sanity).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T12:24:08-07:00","id":904353,"title":"","content":"I think it's not really all that helpful to look at the ideology of different groups. That only results at endless discussions that lead nowhere. It's better to look at their goals. What do they want to achieve? In the old vampire it was pretty clear that the goal of the factions was to destroy the other groups. The organisations were at war. In new vampire it isn't as cut and dry. I think the Invictus is mostly about achieving power and money, the Carthians is for vampires who want to shake things up, the Order has members who want to become an \u00fcbervampire (all benefits, no drawbacks), the LS mostly has vampires who want to be conservative or to stay traditional and the Circle wants to get back to a less structured time and remove all restraint. Pretty much that. It is a bit vague to make out, because of the way it is written.<br /> <br /> So to get back to the original question: The appeal is to do all those different things without being tied to a specific clan. You don't have to be a Ventrue to become a powermonger. You can be a Nosferatu or Gangrel powermonger with a different set of powers than the usual suspect Ventrue wearing a business suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:37:39-07:00","id":904550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcaneumkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm#post893555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, to tell everyone the truth I know very little of Requiem, I know that the Clans are a lot less important to the game and that Sects or Covenants play a more important role in a vampire existence. It's just the way I see it, everything you do in Requiem could be re-created in Masquerade. Although the Sabbat is there as a lurking enemy if playing a Camarilla game, in the end, well in most of the game I've played, you are mostly left to your own device as long as you don't interfere with the prince plans, don't break the masquerade and don't embrace without permission, you are free to do whatever you please. But it seem to me that, I just finish reading 1st edition part of the Covenant, and they come off to me as well, fanatic and I find them to very restricting and uninteresting.<br /> <br /> First you have;<br /> <br /> Carthian Movement: So basically is you hate status quo, and you want thing to change with a burning Ire you join this group.<br /> <br /> But what happens when you start getting power and feel that you might enjoy a bit of status quo in your life ? Your sect tell you, sorry man, but no status quo in this bitch, so you move on the Invictus... ?<br /> <br /> Then<br /> <br /> The Circle of Crone - bunch of Wackos venerating woman and deity who have been shun for their action and or belief and believe in creation so they are probably tending garden ( WTF !) or breeding animals or artist.<br /> <br /> Third<br /> <br /> Invictus - Seem to be written from without, with little to give, they pretty much tell you forward that your chance of increasing into the rank are slim to none, but you can try and until you do, you will be our pawn. - Some would say well camarilla isn't different, yeah, you don't need to be a prince to be powerful. In Masquerade, the Ventrue clan, protect their own, and don't have that stupid restrain oh, don't use technology like computer and cellphone and email, use messenger, its the tradition.<br /> <br /> Then<br /> <br /> Lancea Sanctum - OK so we are fanatic catholic offshoot clan which reject humanity and assume the monster that we are, and human are cattle.<br /> <br /> They enforce/preach their faith, through violence if necessary, but oh wait what if our number are not great enough to convert the enemy, OK then will wait until we do. So if you want to be a religious fanatic with for a progenitor, the roman soldier that killed Christ, we got you covered.<br /> <br /> and Finally<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> Which attempt to transcend the vampiric state, and become something else superior.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and if you do not choose then you are unaligned and then everyone think of you like a bitch or less.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>So tell me Fan of VTR what exactly is it that makes VTR Covenant more interesting that VTM and its 2 Sect ? </b><br /> <br /> From where I am standing it seem a lot more limiting a setting than VTM was.. It was already hard sometime in my opinion to have all players find a reason for their character from different clan working together, now with so many different Sect/covenant, Not only are they probably from different clan but probably from different Sect which will probably not appreciate them aiding and or working with each other. All the while, I feel the clans have taken such a step back that I don't really see the point aside from each of them having a signature discipline and weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well you may want to know that the covenants as they're given in the core book are actually extremely abridged versions. I learned that the hard way by poking around these forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Carthians don't exactly hate the status quo, they want to update it to a form that's more relevant to modern day vampires. They can function as a democracy, republic, possibly even communism. The point is that they're the more liberal and forward thinking covenant.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone are neo pagans who practice an amalgamation of old world religions. They're not all part of the same cult and may not even all worship The Crone. Indeed, some worship other deities such as those of ancient Greece or Egypt.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Invictus are essentially the Requiem's version of the Camarilla. Hell, they even state that they derived from them. So if you want to play as traditionalist vampires where the elders subjugate the neonates, then there you go.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum believe that it is their purpose in God's plan to take on Satan's role on earth. That is to say, their purpose is to test the faithful and punish the wicked. The Lancea Sanctum is actually very protective of devout Christians while terrorizing heretics and sinners.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul seek to become perfect beings, which a lot of people might aspire to be. And even better, it seems that may be a possibility since they have a way to lessen the impacts of the vampire curse. What vampire wouldn't be happy keeping all their powers while still being able to walk in daylight and eat solid foods without vomiting?<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason why remaining unaligned is considered crazy is because life as a vampire is about as dangerous as a Saw movie. Refusing to join a covenant means you don't have strict rules to follow, but it also means that you're on your own if you get into trouble. At least if you join a covenant, you have allies to support you if things go south.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-31-2016, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T01:07:20-07:00","id":904779,"title":"","content":"They aren't better. Just different.<br /> <br /> They each give the game something different to the other, both good and bad.<br /> <br /> Some folks will have preferences, and that's fine, but there is nothing intrinsically better about one than the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6009-nathanb","name":"NathanB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T01:36:17-07:00","id":904788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NathanB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=904779#post904779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't better. Just different.<br /> <br /> They each give the game something different to the other, both good and bad.<br /> <br /> Some folks will have preferences, and that's fine, but there is nothing intrinsically better about one than the other.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/oPlb1pw.webm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/oPlb1pw.webm\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/oPlb1pw.webm\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i.imgur.com/oPlb1pw.webm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T22:25:13-07:00","id":905414,"title":"","content":"Actually I have a question. Kind of a Tangent, but not by much; mostly focused on The Lancea. How do they view morally upright people who aren't Christian? Like for example a Buddhist Monk who's respectful and helps around the community?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:43:37-07:00","id":905450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=905414#post905414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I have a question. Kind of a Tangent, but not by much; mostly focused on The Lancea. How do they view morally upright people who aren't Christian? Like for example a Buddhist Monk who's respectful and helps around the community?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would vary a lot. In Modern Nights though, worrying about that as opposed to the evidence of manifest human wickedness all around them would generally be viewed as bizarre priorities - but you'll find some Elders from the Middle Ages who are still concerned about human degredation through &quot;heresy&quot; who might specifically embrace religious fanatics to carry out that &quot;Crusade&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, they're generally going to be a lot more concerned about Vampire-heretics against the Chapel and Lance, then human religion at all. Afterall they're not even actually Christians themselves in any meaningful sense of the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:05:06-07:00","id":905931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/893555-vtr-fans-please-explain-how-the-covenant-from-vtr-are-better-than-the-sects-from-vtm?p=893591#post893591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sects in Masquerade were all about choosing sides in an ancient war between, and about whether or not you wanted to cling to your Humanity. Requiem has moved away from the former and emphasized the latter, with the Covenants existing primarily as support structures for campires to hold onto through the long eternity of unlife. Covenants shape the beliefs that help keep someone relatively sane as they spend an immortal lifespan as a cruel predator, without which they would quickly fall to the Beast and become a ravening monster. Thr Covenants are there to answer the question of &quot;what do I do now?&quot;<br /> <br /> For the Invictus and Carthians, the answer they provide is political. The Invictus sees opportunity in their unnaturally long lives, pursuing worldly influence and wealth through the long night of the Kindred experience; they also focus on maintaining their Humanity with oaths of obligation and with petty politics, zooming in on ultimately meaningless titles as a distraction from being a mindless hungry beast. The Carthians hone in on mortal feelings of oppression and injustice, allowing passionate and politically active Kindred an outlet for their fury and frustration that isn't just murder and anarchy in the streets; it gives them hope for a better future with less social heirarchy and perhaps even a chance to do away with the Masquerade and return to something resembling normalcy.<br /> <br /> For the Lancea Sanctum and Circle of the Crone, the answer they provide is spiritual. The Embrace is a jarring, horrifying experience, and many feel lost as they must now turn to actions they would've found morally reprehensible in life in order to survive. Both of these Sects explain that it's okay go be a monster, assuaging feelings of guilt with either a divine purpose from the God Himself or a more general pagan belief structure that varies wildly. It's about acceptance and religious succor, distracting the hungry Beast with a new goal in (un)life and a new dogma to base one's identity and actions around.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul are the odd ones out in this equation, and are the smallest Covenant because of this. Rather than pretend at being human like the political factions or embrace the Kindred faiths, they instead fixate on the transformative act of the Embrace and seek to change themselves even further, but this time under their own direct guidance. The Ordo offers control, freeing a vampire to try and shape their own existence with hard work and giving them a goal to strive towards.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a more VtM-centric answer, I'd have to say that it had one interesting Sect - the Sabbat - while the Camarilla and Anarchs were played as both the boring default option (compare the number of clans and bloodlines in the Sabbat to those of the Cammies) and as the idiotic dupes of the setting (who bury their heads in the sand and pretend Gehenna isn't real) - while VtR presents all five Covenants as being equally compelling, diverse, and storied. Another major benefit is that you can bring together a coterie across Covenant lines, because they're all competing belief systems rather than outright warring factions; that tension offers far more story potential than &quot;if you see the other team, you kill them on sight.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200batamajakki, you hit the nail on the head! I agree with this post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}